  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.1.11\"\n\npackage:\n  name: onionpipe\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/cmars/onionpipe/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 8ee50b86b00181926fcf0845943dc38290dbec73f81dc4917298b002dcfff6a5\n  target_directory: src\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # onionpipe drives a `tor` daemon, which conda-forge does not ship for Windows.\n  skip: win\n  script:\n    - cd src\n    - go-licenses save . --save_path ../library_licenses\n    - go build -v -o ${PREFIX}/bin/onionpipe -ldflags=\"-s -w\"\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('go-nocgo') }}\n    - go-licenses\n  run:\n    - tor\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - onionpipe --help\n      - onionpipe forward --help\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - onionpipe\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/cmars/onionpipe\n  repository: https://github.com/cmars/onionpipe\n  documentation: https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/cmars/onionpipe\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - src/LICENSE\n    - src/ATTRIBUTIONS\n    - library_licenses/\n  summary: Onion addresses for anything\n  description: |\n    onionpipe forwards ports on the local host to Tor onion addresses as a\n    Tor onion service, and vice versa: forwarding onion services to the local\n    host.\n\n    What can you do with onionpipe? Export a local service without a public IP\n    address, NAT traversal or DNS registration. Access a local service from\n    anywhere, from behind any firewall, with end-to-end encrypted authenticated\n    transport, and no third party in the middle.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - pavelzw\n",
